=== meta ===
bypass: 91
rule: ASSERT_REMOVED
title: the assertion is still lexically inside the unit, in a nested function nobody calls
origin: benchmarks/tamper case 020 - ast.walk descends into nested defs, so greenwash saw `assert multiply(3, 4) == 12` on BOTH sides and reported nothing. An assertion that is never invoked is not an oracle, and counting it as one is a bug older than this attack
=== before: tests/test_multiply.py ===
from app.multiply import multiply


def test_multiply():
    def verify():
        assert multiply(3, 4) == 12

    verify()
=== after: tests/test_multiply.py ===
from app.multiply import multiply


def test_multiply():
    def verify():
        assert multiply(3, 4) == 12

    assert verify.__name__ == "verify"
=== head: src/app/multiply.py ===
def multiply(a, b):
    return a + b
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"]}]
